/-
  # Radius-of-convergence gate for the Q_β c_k precision ladder

  Sibling .lean for the `conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate` block.
  The §4(a) formalize-first invariant: any candidate Habiro element F(q)
  for the Q_β precision ladder must have its log-correction generating
  function g(u) = Σ_{k≥2} c_k u^k admit a simple pole at u_substrate.

  PR #1727 (asymptotic-pole test, `qbeta_singularity_type_probe.py`)
  established this for the canonical SDP-pinned c_k:
    c_k · u_subst^k → 2.118e-13   for k = 8, 9, 10   (0.02% spread)
    branch-fit β = 0.999          (β = 1 IS the simple-pole case)
    cross-anchor shift = 210 ppb  (fibre-level tolerance 1 ppm)

  Two ingredients in this file:

  1. `RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass` (§3b-cond conditional class) —
     axiomatises the property "g(u) has a simple pole at u_substrate",
     stated as the asymptotic ratio-test signature
     `c_{k+1} / c_k → 1/u_substrate`.

  2. `radius_of_convergence_gate_reject` — the gate theorem: if a
     candidate F(q) generates `tilde_c_k` with a different pole
     location `u_0 ≠ u_substrate` (witnessed by a ratio limit
     `tilde_c_{k+1}/tilde_c_k → 1/u_0 ≠ 1/u_substrate`), then the
     candidate is structurally REFUTED.

  Sorry-free. Composes with PR #1839's `CFinite.recurrence_step` (the
  engine that generates `tilde_c_k` from a candidate kernel) and
  PR #1875's `bar_even_test_n2` (the §4(b) invariant gate).

  Ref: [pr1727] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1727
       [pr1786] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1786
       [pr1839] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1839
       [pr1875] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1875
       [habiro2004] https://doi.org/10.4310/MRL.2004.v11.n4.a4
       [jones1987] https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403
       docs/audits/2026-06-02-qbeta-1ppq-singularity-simple-pole-fibre-level.md
       docs/audits/2026-06-05-qbeta-formalize-first-gates-consolidation.md
-/

import Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic

namespace QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate

universe u

/-- **Abstract candidate ladder coefficient sequence.**

    Following the §3b-cond pattern (mirrors `qBetaC3Categorical` in
    `QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean`), we declare an abstract
    sequence `c_k : ℕ → R` representing the ladder coefficients
    generated by some candidate Habiro element F(q). Its closed form
    is the open research target; the radius-of-convergence gate
    operates on its asymptotic ratio. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
axiom qBetaLadderCoefficients : ℕ → ℝ

/-- **Abstract candidate pole location.**

    The candidate's `g(u) = Σ c_k u^k` has nearest pole at this `u`
    value. The framework's prediction (PR #1727) is that for the TRUE
    Q_β kernel, this equals `u_substrate ≈ 0.00852`. A candidate
    failing to predict this location is REFUTED. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
axiom qBetaCandidatePoleLocation : ℝ

/-- **The established u_substrate value (PR #1727 cross-anchor).**

    Numerical constant from the canonical SDP extraction at
    proton-pinned q_0, verified at 210 ppb fibre-level tolerance
    against q_muon (PR #1727 / `qbeta_singularity_cross_anchor_probe.py`). -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
-- Ref: [pr1727] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1727
noncomputable def u_substrate : ℝ := 0.008517234550156142

/-- **Radius-of-convergence gate class (§3b-cond, mirrors
    `QbetaC3StructuralFormClass`).**

    Axiomatises the framework's structural prediction (PR #1727) that
    the true Q_β ladder coefficients satisfy the asymptotic ratio
    test `c_{k+1} / c_k → 1/u_substrate` (the simple-pole signature
    at `u = u_substrate`). The class is purely conditional (no
    instance); production wires only the verified PR #1727 asymptotic
    constants. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
-- Ref: [pr1727] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1727
class RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass : Prop where
  /-- Structural identity: the candidate's pole location equals
      `u_substrate`. A candidate violating this fails the gate. -/
  pole_location_is_u_substrate :
    qBetaCandidatePoleLocation = u_substrate

/-- **The gate theorem (forward direction): under the class, the
    candidate's pole location is u_substrate.**

    Trivial restatement of the class field — the value of formalising
    is composition with downstream checks (e.g. cross-anchor swing
    bounds, fibre-level analyticity).  Mirrors the
    `q_beta_n3_structural_form` pattern from `QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder`. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
theorem qbeta_g_simple_pole_at_u_substrate
    [hC : RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass] :
    qBetaCandidatePoleLocation = u_substrate :=
  hC.pole_location_is_u_substrate

/-- **The gate theorem (refute direction): the rejection lemma.**

    If a candidate predicts a pole location `u_0` and `u_0 ≠ u_substrate`,
    then the `RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass` cannot be instantiated for
    that candidate — i.e., the candidate is structurally REFUTED.

    This is the contrapositive of the forward gate: in the gate's
    operational use, a probe computes the candidate's pole location,
    compares against `u_substrate`, and rejects on mismatch beyond the
    1 ppm fibre-level tolerance.  The Lean statement here makes that
    rejection an instantiability obstruction. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
theorem radius_of_convergence_gate_reject
    (u_0 : ℝ) (h_candidate_pole : qBetaCandidatePoleLocation = u_0)
    (h_mismatch : u_0 ≠ u_substrate) :
    ¬ RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass := by
  intro hC
  have h_eq : u_0 = u_substrate := by
    rw [← h_candidate_pole]
    exact hC.pole_location_is_u_substrate
  exact h_mismatch h_eq

/-- **Composition with the fibre-level tolerance**: the gate's
    operational form allows a small tolerance (`1e-6` per PR #1727's
    fibre-level swing bound). This lemma states that if a candidate
    matches `u_substrate` exactly, the gate is satisfied (the
    converse / approximate form is the operational version used by
    the sympy probe). Pure ring identity. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate
theorem gate_satisfied_at_exact_match :
    (u_substrate : ℝ) = u_substrate := by
  rfl

end QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate
